    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11682" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Croesus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κροῖσος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of Lydia, celebrated for his
				riches</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 19, 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin.
				2, 27, 87</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 11,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 1, 7, 2</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Prop. 2</span></i>
			(3), 26, 23 al.— Appel. for <i>a rich
			man</i>, in contrast with Irus, <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 3,
				7, 42</span></i>; and in plur., <i><span class="en">Mart. 11,
				6, 4</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Croesĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of Crœsus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6, § 578</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
